<div class="ls-story-unit" data-tone="teal" data-watermark="planes">
<div class="ls-container">
<div class="ls-principle-pair">
<article class="ls-principle" data-principle="true" id="quiet">
<span class="ls-principle-index">07 /</span>
<h3>LET NOTHING HAPPEN.</h3>
<p>No meaningful change is a useful result. A failed source is an exception to explain. A fluent rewrite is not proof of progress. Judge continuing work by the attention it saves, not the amount of text it produces.</p>
</article>
<article class="ls-principle" data-principle="true" id="review">
<span class="ls-principle-index">08 /</span>
<h3>KEEP THE FINAL WORD.</h3>
<p>Automation can do the upkeep. You decide what to keep. Flow’s Morning Briefing brings changed parts together for review, with Keep and Revert. A trustworthy routine makes recovery part of the experience.</p>
</article>
</div>
